# Mobile list pagination

Native collection screens in the Expo app use **on-scroll pagination only** — no pager controls. Append the next page when the user scrolls near the bottom of `FeatureScreen`.

Skill: [item-list skill](../skills/item-list/SKILL.md). Hooks live in `mobile/src/shared/hooks/`.

## Required pieces

| Piece | Source |
|-------|--------|
| Page wrapper | `FeatureScreen` with `onScroll={onScroll}` and scroll content `flex-grow` |
| List body | `ListPageBody` wrapping list + footer (`flex-1` column) |
| List footer | `ListPageFooter` below `ItemList` / list component (`mt-auto`) |
| Scroll handler | `useListPageScroll` → `useScrollLoadMore` from `@webonone/mobile-ui` |
| Server pages | `useServerPaginatedList` |
| Client slice | `useClientInfiniteList` (full array already in memory) |

**Forbidden on native list pages:** `Pagination` from `@webonone/mobile-ui` (kit showcase may still demo the control in Components).

## Defaults

| Setting | Value |
|---------|--------|
| Initial `pageSize` | **12** (`DEFAULT_LIST_PAGE_SIZE`) |
| Queue / history API lists | **24** when the screen passes `pageSize: 24` to the hook |

Filter or search change → page 1 **replace**. Near-bottom scroll → **append** next page.

## Server-paginated API

Use when the backend returns `{ items, total, page, pageSize }`.

```tsx
const list = useServerPaginatedList({
  fetchPage: async (query) => {
    const result = await myApi.list({
      page: Number(query.page ?? 1),
      pageSize: Number(query.pageSize ?? 12),
      q: query.q as string | undefined,
      status: String(query.status ?? 'all'),
    })
    return {
      items: result.items,
      total: result.total,
      page: result.page,
      pageSize: result.pageSize,
    }
  },
})
const onScroll = useListPageScroll(list)

return (
  <FeatureScreen title="…" onScroll={onScroll}>
    <ListPageBody>
      <MyList items={list.items} />
      <ListPageFooter
        loadedCount={list.items.length}
        totalCount={list.total}
        hasMore={list.hasMore}
        loadingMore={list.loadingMore}
      />
    </ListPageBody>
  </FeatureScreen>
)
```

Search: `list.searchQuery` + `list.setSearchQuery`. Extra filters: `list.patchQueryParams({ status: value })`. After mutations: `list.reload()`.

Reference: `SalesHistoryScreen.tsx`, `InvoicesScreen.tsx`, `sms/screens/HistoryScreen.tsx`.

## Client-sliced lists

Use when the screen loads the full array once and filters in memory (companies, themes, templates).

```tsx
const pagination = useClientInfiniteList(filteredItems, 12, resetKey)
const onScroll = useListPageScroll(pagination)

<ListPageBody>
  <MyList items={pagination.visibleItems} />
  <ListPageFooter
    loadedCount={pagination.loadedCount}
    totalCount={pagination.totalCount}
    hasMore={pagination.hasMore}
    loadingMore={pagination.loadingMore}
  />
</ListPageBody>
```

Pass a `resetKey` (e.g. search query string) so scroll position resets when filters change.

Reference: `AllCompaniesScreen.tsx`, `SystemThemeScreen.tsx`, `sms/screens/TemplatesScreen.tsx`.

## Data catalog helper

Entity list screens may use `usePaginatedEntityList` in `mobile/src/features/data/hooks/` — it wraps `useServerPaginatedList` with Data API query params.

## Small static lists

Screens that always return a short fixed set (e.g. SMS devices) may omit `ListPageFooter` when pagination adds no value.

## Verification

```bash
npm run type-check -w @webonone/mobile-ui
npm run type-check -w @webonone/mobile
```

Confirm no `Pagination` import under `mobile/src/features/**` except kit `ComponentsShowcase`.
